From: christopherrobertbrooks-tech
 <289533927+christopherrobertbrooks-tech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:21:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fold the attention score scale into q_norm in float16 (XL
 models overflow in eager attention)

The XL checkpoints' decoder.layers.0 q_norm/k_norm weights reach ~31.6 each, so eager attention's unscaled
matmul(q, k^T) can reach ~128,000 -- past float16's 65,504 -- and every latent turns NaN on pre-Ampere GPUs.
Multiplying q_norm.weight by 1/sqrt(head_dim) and setting scaling to 1.0 gives the same scores, already scaled,
straight out of the matmul (RoPE is a rotation, so it commutes). No runtime cost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
